
---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About MyRigFoundry | Meet the Founder"
  description="Meet Leonardo Ribeiro, the founder of MyRigFoundry, an independent project focused on PC troubleshooting, hardware and technology."
>
  <section class="info-page">
    <div class="info-container">
      <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT MYRIGFOUNDRY</p>

      <h1>Built from curiosity. Driven by technology.</h1>

      <p class="info-lead">
        MyRigFoundry is an independent technology project created by
        Leonardo Ribeiro. It combines an interest in computers,
        software development and the desire to make technical
        information easier to understand.
      </p>

      <div class="info-content">
        <h2>Meet the founder</h2>

        <p>
          Hi, I'm Leonardo Ribeiro, the creator of MyRigFoundry.
          I'm currently studying Systems Analysis and Development
          at PUCRS, in Brazil, while developing my skills in
          software development and technology.
        </p>

        <p>
          My interest in technology goes beyond writing code.
          I've always been curious about how computers work,
          why technical problems happen and how the right
          information can help people solve them.
        </p>

        <p>
          MyRigFoundry started as a personal project and became
          an opportunity to bring together these interests:
          building a website, researching PC-related topics
          and creating practical content for other computer users.
        </p>

        <div class="founder-links">
          <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/leonardo-ribeiro-834907409/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Connect with me on LinkedIn →
          </a>
        </div>

        <h2>Why I created MyRigFoundry</h2>

        <p>
          Finding reliable information about a PC problem can
          be frustrating. Some explanations are too technical,
          while others skip important details and jump straight
          to recommending new hardware.
        </p>

        <p>
          I wanted to build a resource that approaches these
          problems differently: explaining what might be
          happening, showing how to investigate possible causes
          and helping readers make informed decisions.
        </p>

        <h2>What I work on</h2>

        <p>
          I manage the development and maintenance of MyRigFoundry,
          including its website, content structure, research
          and publishing process.
        </p>

        <p>
          The website is built with Astro and focuses on topics such as:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Windows troubleshooting and PC performance.</li>
          <li>SSD, HDD and storage problems.</li>
          <li>Networking and connectivity.</li>
          <li>RAM, BIOS and hardware compatibility.</li>
          <li>Graphics cards, monitors and PC components.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Understand it. Fix it. Upgrade it.</h2>

        <div class="info-principles">
          <div class="info-principle">
            <span>01</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Understand it</h3>
              <p>
                Understand the symptoms and possible causes
                before making changes to your computer.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="info-principle">
            <span>02</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Fix it</h3>
              <p>
                Follow clear troubleshooting steps and learn
                how to investigate common PC problems.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="info-principle">
            <span>03</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Upgrade it</h3>
              <p>
                Make better hardware decisions based on actual
                needs rather than unnecessary purchases.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>An ongoing project</h2>

        <p>
          MyRigFoundry is constantly evolving. As I continue
          studying, learning and developing new skills, I also
          work to improve the website and the information
          available to its readers.
        </p>

        <p>
          This is more than a website. It's a personal project
          where I can apply what I learn, explore technology
          and build something useful.
        </p>

        <p>
          Thanks for visiting MyRigFoundry.
        </p>

        <p>
          Have a question, suggestion or correction?
          <a href="/contact/">Get in touch.</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
